<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    What happens at a point: a blast, fragments, something left lying on the
    ground, or any mix of them. Each <effect> here has a name, and anything
    that goes off runs it by that name:

        projectiles.xml   <onDestroy><effect key="frag_blast"/></onDestroy>
        objects.xml       <onDestroy><effect key="c4_blast"/></onDestroy>
        agents/*.xml      <onDeath><effect key="ghoul_burst"/></onDeath>
        Lua scripts       { effect = "toxic_gas", at = "player" }  (quest-authoring.md)

    so a gas cloud written once can be a grenade, a barrel that leaks when it
    is shot, a ghoul that bursts on death, or a quest's trap.

    A reference can change the effect for that one use without copying it.
    Child elements merge into the effect's own, attribute by attribute:

        <effect key="toxic_gas"><zone tiles="60" holdMs="20000"/></effect>

    is toxic_gas, twice as big and lasting twice as long. A <client> look is
    the effect's and is not changed by an override.

    The parts can also still be written inline, straight into <onDestroy> or
    <onDeath>, as before this file existed. Inline parts run first, then each
    <effect> in order. An inline zone has no <client> look of its own: clients
    draw it by its kind.

    <effect key="..." clientEffectId="N">
        key            the name everything else uses.
        clientEffectId what a zone of this effect is called on the wire, so a
                       client draws it with this entry's <client> look.
                       Required, unique, from 1. Never renumber one in use.

    In an effect, in the order they run:

    <explosion area= radius= playerDamage= buildingDamage= knockback= throughWall=>
        <onHit condition= chance= durationMs= strength=/>
    </explosion>
        A blast. `area` tiles round the tile it went off on (area="1" is
        3x3), else a circle of `radius` world units. playerDamage to every
        player and agent in it, buildingDamage to every building and
        resource. throughWall (0..1, default 0): the share of damage,
        knockback and condition chance that reaches a creature with a wall,
        rock or tree between it and the blast. 0 means cover protects
        completely. Buildings are never sheltered. <onHit> is what the blast
        inflicts on every creature it catches (conditions.xml).

    <fragments projectile="frag_fragment" count="22" range="400" damage="40"
               buildingDamage="40" knockback="0" speedMultiplier="1.0"
               spread="1" rangeVariation="0.6" speedVariation="0.4" falloff="0.4"/>
        A frag's fragments. `count` (at most 48) REAL projectiles of the
        `projectile` entry of projectiles.xml fly out of the blast, one
        somewhere in each slice of the circle (`spread`, 0..1, is how much of
        its slice it may wander over). Each falls up to `rangeVariation`
        (0..0.9) short of `range` (at most 2000) and flies up to
        `speedVariation` (0..0.9) slower than the fastest, so the burst is
        ragged rather than a ring. Each one flies, collides and is drawn
        exactly like a bullet: it stops at the first wall, rock, tree, player
        or ghoul in its way, which takes `damage` (the fragment's <damage
        type>, so armour counts) or, for buildings and resources,
        `buildingDamage` (the same as `damage` unless stated). `falloff`
        (0..1, default 1 = none) is the share of both still done by a
        fragment landing at `range`. Nothing protects whoever set it off from
        their own. A blast against a wall loses the fragments heading into
        it; the rest fly out from its face. The fastest fly at the fragment
        entry's <physics baseSpeed> times speedMultiplier.

    <zone kind="gas|smoke|fire" tiles="30" radius="" growMs="3000" holdMs="10000"
          fadeMs="3000" tickMs="500" damage="6" damageType="gas"
          buildingDamage="0" burns="wood,cloth" blocksVision=""
          shape="fill" stretch="1" forward="0" irregular="0" blockedBy="walls">
        <onHit condition="choking"/>
        <onEnd effect="..."/>
    </zone>
        Something left lying on the ground (<cloud> is the same element under
        its old name). It spreads over at most `tiles` tiles (up to 255),
        nearest first, within `radius` tiles (default: what `tiles` covers as
        a disc plus one; at most 12). It grows over growMs, stays holdMs,
        thins out over fadeMs (each at most 60000).

        Damage. Every tickMs while grown or holding, each player and ghoul
        standing in it takes `damage` of `damageType` (a wearable's
        <modifier key="gasResistance"> reduces "gas", fireResistance "fire")
        and gets the <onHit> condition. buildingDamage, burns: every tick,
        each building on or right next to a covered tile whose material is
        listed in `burns` takes buildingDamage (fire burns a wooden wall, not
        a stone one). An object's material is its material= in objects.xml,
        or read off its <client particles=>.

        Sight. blocksVision (default true for kind="smoke", false otherwise):
        while it is there, until half faded, nobody is sent a player, ghoul
        or anything else that moves if the line to it crosses from clear air
        into the zone or back - from outside you see neither into nor past
        it, and from inside you see only the inside. Ghouls cannot target
        through it either. It gives its tiles back last-grown first over the
        first half of the fade, so it shrinks to where it went off.

        Shape. Without anything set it is round. Something that was moving
        when it went off (a thrown grenade or bottle) has a direction:
          shape="fill" stretch="2"   twice as long ALONG that direction as
                                     across it: a splash running on.
          shape="line" stretch="3"   three times as long ACROSS it: a wall
                                     laid in front of the thrower. A line
                                     is stretch 3 unless stated.
          forward="1.5"              its middle that many tiles further on
                                     along the direction (negative: back).
        stretch is 1..6. Something that went off where it lay - a dead ghoul,
        a destroyed barrel, a grenade dropped at someone's feet - has no
        direction, and is round whatever these say.
        irregular (0..1) roughens the edge, differently every time.
        blockedBy is what it cannot spread through: "walls" (walls and closed
        doors: what stops a bullet; the default), "walls,scenery" (rocks and
        trees too), or "none" (only the edge of the map). Doors opened later
        do not let it out: the shape is fixed when it goes off.

        Merging. A gas or fire zone landing on one of the same effect that
        is still burning does not lie on top of it: it feeds it. The first
        takes in the new one's tiles and starts its hold again, and the
        latest thrower gets the kills, so five molotovs on one spot are one
        fire. Zones that block vision always stay separate.

        <onEnd effect="..."/>: another effect, run where the zone started
        once it is gone. Takes overrides like any reference.

    <effect key="..."/>
        Another effect, run after this one's own parts, at the same point.
        Takes overrides like any reference.

    <client .../>
        How this effect's zone is drawn. Looks only: nothing here changes
        what anyone is sent or what the zone does.
          render="puff"   soft puffs over every tile (gas, smoke).
              color="r,g,b"      the puffs' colour.
              alpha="0.42"       how thick at full strength (0..1).
              insideAlpha="0.3"  how thick while you stand in a zone that
                                 blocks vision: thin enough to see who is in
                                 there with you.
              size="0.85"        each puff's radius, in tiles.
              drift="12"         how far each puff wanders, in world units.
              maskColor="r,g,b" maskAlpha="0.94"
                                 the darkness over everything outside a zone
                                 that blocks vision, while you stand in it.
          render="fire"   flames, smoke, embers, light and scorch.
              flameColors="#d9573b,#ee8f45,#f2cf68"
                                 the three flame layers, outermost first.
              smokeColor="r,g,b" smokeLitColor="r,g,b"
                                 the fire's smoke and its lit top.
              emberColor="r,g,b" its sparks.
              shatter="true"     a bottle breaking (glass, a fireball) when it
                                 starts; false for a fire nothing threw.
          render="none"   not drawn at all.
        A zone with no look (written inline, or an effect without <client>)
        is drawn by its kind: gas green, smoke grey, fire as a molotov's.

    Every number is a starting point for playtesting, not a decision.
-->
<effects>

    <!-- Grenades. -->

    <!-- The offensive grenade: a big blast and shove, nothing that flies. -->
    <effect key="offensive_blast" clientEffectId="1">
        <explosion area="1" playerDamage="200" buildingDamage="400" knockback="20">
            <onHit condition="slowed" chance="1" durationMs="600" strength="0.2"/>
        </explosion>
    </effect>

    <!-- The frag: a small blast and a ring of fragments. Lethal in the open,
         survivable behind anything solid. -->
    <effect key="frag_blast" clientEffectId="2">
        <explosion radius="90" playerDamage="40" buildingDamage="30" knockback="4"/>
        <fragments projectile="frag_fragment" count="22" range="400" damage="40" buildingDamage="40"
                   spread="1" rangeVariation="0.6" speedVariation="0.4" falloff="0.4"/>
    </effect>

    <!-- Gas: no blast at all. A cloud that fills a room or a corridor and
         hurts whoever stays in it. -->
    <effect key="toxic_gas" clientEffectId="3">
        <zone kind="gas" tiles="30" growMs="3000" holdMs="10000" fadeMs="3000"
              tickMs="500" damage="6" damageType="gas">
            <onHit condition="choking"/>
        </zone>
        <client render="puff" color="150,178,52" alpha="0.42"/>
    </effect>

    <!-- Smoke: no blast, no damage. A thick cloud nobody can see into, out
         of or through; the server stops sending what it hides. -->
    <effect key="smoke_screen" clientEffectId="4">
        <zone kind="smoke" tiles="40" growMs="2000" holdMs="15000" fadeMs="4000"/>
        <client render="puff" color="170,170,170" alpha="0.85" insideAlpha="0.3"
                maskColor="48,48,48" maskAlpha="0.94"/>
    </effect>

    <!-- The molotov's fire: a patch that burns whoever stands in it, keeps
         burning them a moment after they leave (burning), and eats wooden
         buildings next to it. Stone and metal do not burn. -->
    <effect key="molotov_fire" clientEffectId="5">
        <zone kind="fire" tiles="9" radius="2" growMs="500" holdMs="8000" fadeMs="1500"
              tickMs="500" damage="8" damageType="fire" buildingDamage="90" burns="wood,cloth">
            <onHit condition="burning"/>
        </zone>
        <client render="fire" shatter="true"/>
    </effect>

    <!-- Placed explosives (objects.xml). -->

    <effect key="landmine_blast" clientEffectId="6">
        <explosion area="1" playerDamage="200" buildingDamage="400" knockback="20">
            <onHit condition="slowed" chance="1" durationMs="1000" strength="1.0"/>
        </explosion>
    </effect>

    <effect key="dynamite_blast" clientEffectId="7">
        <explosion area="1" playerDamage="180" buildingDamage="1400" knockback="20">
            <onHit condition="slowed" chance="1" durationMs="1000" strength="1.0"/>
        </explosion>
    </effect>

    <effect key="c4_blast" clientEffectId="8">
        <explosion area="1" playerDamage="255" buildingDamage="6000" knockback="20">
            <onHit condition="slowed" chance="1" durationMs="2000" strength="1.5"/>
        </explosion>
    </effect>

    <!-- A fuel barrel going up (furnitures.xml). The big one names this with
         a heavier <explosion playerDamage>. -->
    <effect key="barrel_blast" clientEffectId="9">
        <explosion area="1" playerDamage="250" buildingDamage="10000" knockback="20">
            <onHit condition="slowed" chance="1" durationMs="1000" strength="1.0"/>
        </explosion>
    </effect>

    <!-- Agents bursting on death (data/agents). The corpse's, not the
         killer's: see Player::dropGhoulRemains. -->

    <effect key="ghoul_burst" clientEffectId="10">
        <explosion radius="40" playerDamage="120" buildingDamage="500"/>
    </effect>

    <effect key="teslabot_burst" clientEffectId="11">
        <explosion radius="40" playerDamage="100" buildingDamage="100"/>
    </effect>

</effects>
